A||N||6||Slapnutz2000||Rear decklid replacement and battery question||||5||
Z||000000||Slapnutz2000||06-11-2001||01:56 AM||||The left hinge of my rear decklid broke and barely allows me to close the lid completely.  As a result, I am unable to get anything electrical to work (lights won't go up, radio doesn't come on, courtesy lights won't work, etc.) and I believe my battery is dead.<P>I have two questions.<P>1) How much should I expect to pay for a new rear decklid if I take it to PepBoys and how much time should it take to install? Should I buy one from a boneyard and how easy are the decklids to install? (I haven't put one on before)<P>2) Would it be worth it to call AAA and have them try to recharge the battery or should I buy a new one?||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-11-2001||07:52 AM||||I also have a few questions...<P>First off, what year/style decklid?  That will make a difference in price.<P>Second, is the fact that none of your electrical systems work as a result of your decklid hinge being broken, or having a dead battery?  I guess I don't understand how having a broken hinge will make some electrical systems fail.<P>If the decklid is staying open, and draining your battery because of the trunk light, just take the bulb out and get your battery recharged.  If it dosent take a charge or hold it for very long, then you need to buy a new battery.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||gcmrrc||06-11-2001||08:12 AM||||Check fuseible link coming from starter if lights and radio and interior lights don't work||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierojunky||06-11-2001||08:20 AM||||JUST DON'T TAKE IT TO PEPBOYS.  I have had MANY bad experiences with them at several locations with both my car and my truck.  If your interested in the details email me and I'll write them for you.  To long to post here. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||06-11-2001||10:58 AM||||Just from the looks of it, it dosent look to hard at all.  The tension rods are the most difficult, so I have read.  If you dont watch out, you can end up breaking your rear window.  Also, you will need to get a security torx bit for two of the bolts.  If you take a look at them you'll see that it has a normal torx head, but there is a pin in the center of it, thus requiring a special bit.  You can also try to drill the little pin out too.  I dont know what size security torx bit it is though.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||06-11-2001||11:13 AM||||slapnuts:<P>  first off, where are you? maybe someone nearby can help you with parts or hands on repair time.<P>  second. The lid itself comes off easily. two bolts on each side, 13mm, take the lid off.<P>  if your hindge is broken then you have to fight the springs to replace it, more work, more involved.<P>  and it sounds like your electrical problems are from you trunk light staying on, so if you recharge the battery it will most likely be okay. Pull the lamp or wedge something plastic in the switch to keep it locked down.<P>  if you really need a new hinge the best price will be at a junk yard, esp if you find it yourself. Pep boys and those kinds of places are best for oil changes, exhaust, brakes... simple normal maintance things that most people dont do themselves. <P>  Im sure they can fix hindges and stuff like that, but they will be figuring it out as they do it, same as you would have to, and you will be paying them, what? $65 an hour to do so? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Slapnutz2000||06-11-2001||12:47 PM||||Thanks for all the advice, guys! I appreciate it.<P>The battery was drained completely.  I tried to recharge it last night but it will not hold anything.  <P>Also, there is a D-shaped hinge on the left side and the flat top part is broken. That is why my 86 2m4 decklid will not stay closed. I think I can take a 2-3 inch peice of metal and weld it into place to fix the problem.<P>Sorry for not using the correct terminology but I've looked around the Net and I can't find the words.<P>Thanks again!||||reg||14
